content:
HAYS — Great Bend's trio of state-ranked wrestlers earned runner-up finishes at the Bob Kuhn Wrestling Tournament.
In championship matches, No. 6 Triston Tomlinson (20-4, 138) was pinned by Oakley's No. 1 ranked Carter Krier (2:26); No. 3 Jace Schartz (16-3, 165) was pinned by Tripp DuVall of Holly, Colo. (1:29); No. 6 Trenton Kern (11-3, 215) was pinned by Manhattan's No. 3 Landon Dobson (2:35).
No. 5 Cal Schartz (20-5, 113) defeated Hugoton's Isaiah Peachey, 15-0 for third place.
No. 5 Hayden Kelly (15-4, 150) placed third with a victory over St. Francis' No. 5 Dayton Fromholtz 10-3 to beat him for the second time at Hays.
